  "description": "RITFEH crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C64 H103 Er3 Fe7 N22 O27 1+,1.5(C1 H4 O1),7.5(H2 O1),Cl1 1-. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 8 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe3 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe4 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe5 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors; Fe6 (Fe) has 5 O neighbors; Fe7 (Fe) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 19 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.219-3.843 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.16-144.84°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er3Fe7(μ4-O)2(μ3-OH)2(N3)5(MeOH)(mdea)7(PhCO2)4]Cl·7.5H2O·1.5MeOH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
